; WAS a tripwire: generating from this used to FAIL, because an empty `?T` is
; JSON null on the wire and null was also how a failed call reported itself, so
; "found nothing" and "the call failed" were one answer.
;
; It now GENERATES, and the test beside it asserts the two properties that make
; that safe rather than merely permitted:
;
;   * the surface keeps the value type — `std::optional<QString>`, not a bare
;     QVariant, so the empty answer is distinct from ""; and
;   * failure still travels on the ERROR channel, not in the value: a generated
;     body decides nothing from the result's null-ness, and logos::LpClient
;     decides success from the C ABI return code.
;
; The file keeps its name so the history of the rule stays findable from the
; test that used to enforce it.
module refusing_module {
  version "1.0.0"
  method lookup(id: tstr) -> ?tstr
}
